bAI
===

A terminal-based AI coding agent. Single binary, TUI interface.

Status: early development. Core chat loop + coding agent tools work.

Features
--------
- TUI with provider and model selection
- Streaming chat against OpenAI, Anthropic, or Groq (any
  OpenAI-compatible endpoint via config)
- SQLite-backed sessions (conversations)
- File read/write/edit tools
- Bash command execution
- Diff view of file changes
- OpenCode variant support

Requirements
------------
- Go 1.26+
- An API key for at least one supported provider

Build
-----
    make build     build the binary into bin/bai
    make run       build and run
    make test      run the test suite
    make clean     remove build artifacts

Config
------
Config lives at ~/.config/bai/config.json. Copy config.example.json
there and fill in your API keys.

    mkdir -p ~/.config/bai
    cp config.example.json ~/.config/bai/config.json

You can also point to a different file with -config.

Usage
-----
    bai                        use the default config
    bai -config path/to.json   use a specific config

Project layout
--------------
    cmd/bai/         entry point and start command
    internal/agent/  provider gateway and message handling
    internal/tui/    bubble tea model, view, update
    internal/db/     sqlite connection and queries
    internal/config/ config loading and defaults